					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/alces-alces" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4057128&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1580589796" alt="Alces_alces" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4057128)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/alces-alces" >Alces_alces</a></span> for the help conceptualizing and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rounderhouse" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4187885&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1580589796" alt="Rounderhouse" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4187885)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rounderhouse" >Rounderhouse</a></span> for helping me put the image together. Original photo was taken by me today at an Atari museum I stumbled across in a flea market. It's an error screen from a Galaga '88 arcade cabinet.</p> <p>This is a Fifth Church GoI Format from the perspective of someone involved with <span style="color: purple">Arcadia</span> another set of weird magic users seen in <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1070">SCP-1070</a>, <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2600">SCP-2600</a>, and <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4564">SCP-4564</a></p> 
